{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":24,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":false,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":1061,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1754071,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":257115,"Name":"Melissa14","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257115.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":true},"StartDate":1367600506,"LastPoster":{"Id":279867,"Name":"cfinkenbine","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279867.jpg?_r=1411696267","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":275,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":29,"Preview":{"Id":1754071,"PostDate":1367600506,"PostContent":"With 85 days until my wedding (thank you theknot.com for reminding me) I am having major packing...","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><em><span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span>Marrying My 5th Grade \"Boyfriend\"...Life has a funny way of working itself out <span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"trina2103@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"98.154.15.214","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1340652630,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257115.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Melissa14","Id":257115,"Name":"Melissa14","IsOnline":true}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b86ea8177c5295bc2c8ae05892cb9460","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; With 85 days until my wedding (thank you theknot.com for reminding me) I am having major packing anxiety. As I gather all the OOT bag stuff and decorations in a designated WEDDING STUFF ONLY AREA under my staircase I cannot help but panic. Apparently Alaska Airlines charges $20 for every single bag that is checked in. I guess that isn&#039;t so bad but I really don&#039;t want to carry\/worry about a million bags all the way to Mexico.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span alt=\":plane:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2131\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/plane.gif\"&gt;&lt;img id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2130\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/plane.gif\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I am totally being dramatic because I might not need a million bags but then what if I do. What if I forget something like THE RINGS! &lt;span alt=\":smile35:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_1422\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile35.gif\"&gt;&lt;img id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_1421\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile35.gif\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Is this normal anxiety? I have a very lengthy packing list but will that help!? Someone help me I am freaking out!&lt;span alt=\":sick:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2600\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sick.gif\"&gt;&lt;img id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2599\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sick.gif\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1754071,"PostDate":1367600506,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> With 85 days until my wedding (thank you theknot.com for reminding me) I am having major packing anxiety. As I gather all the OOT bag stuff and decorations in a designated WEDDING STUFF ONLY AREA under my staircase I cannot help but panic. Apparently Alaska Airlines charges $20 for every single bag that is checked in. I guess that isn't so bad but I really don't want to carry\/worry about a million bags all the way to Mexico.\u00a0 <span alt=\":plane:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2131\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/plane.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2130\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/plane.gif\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I am totally being dramatic because I might not need a million bags but then what if I do. What if I forget something like THE RINGS! <span alt=\":smile35:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_1422\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile35.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_1421\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile35.gif\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Is this normal anxiety? I have a very lengthy packing list but will that help!? Someone help me I am freaking out!<span alt=\":sick:\" id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2600\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sick.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' id=\"yui_3_7_3_1_1367596548839_2599\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/sick.gif\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><em><span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span>Marrying My 5th Grade \"Boyfriend\"...Life has a funny way of working itself out <span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"trina2103@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"98.154.15.214","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1340652630,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257115.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Melissa14","Id":257115,"Name":"Melissa14","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"815911e3da98b2d541b41bee1bb31567","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Totally normal Melissa14!! Try spreading out some of the items between your bridal party (isn&#039;t that what they are there for?!) to lower the number of additional bags you will have to bring. I&#039;ll share with you the packing list that we give to our clients as well so you can cross reference!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Happy Planning!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Carry-on items&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding dress. Don&#039;t trust your dress to checked luggage. Most airplanes have coat closets and will allow travelers to hang garment bags. Call ahead, let them know you will be bringing a dress and ask if the airline will let you hang your dress in the closet&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Groom\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s wedding outfit (tux, suit, shorts, etc.)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;All original and notarized documents--including air tickets, birth certificates, passports, hotel reservation confirmation, medical\/trip insurance, etc.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Two sets of photocopies of all of the above documents&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Your credit cards and ATM cards&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Phone numbers for your doctor, house\/pet sitter and credit card companies (in case your cards are lost or stolen)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Prescription medicine (in the original bottle)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding rings&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding vows&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Your veil&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Bridal jewelry&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A change of clothes for the first day (just in case), including a bathing suit&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Copies of all contracts and vendor contact sheets&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Checked items&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Personal&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Special hosiery or undergarments&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding night sleepwear&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A variety of shoes (flip flops, heels, running shoes\/walking shoes, etc.)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Tiara or headpiece&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Garter&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Sunglasses&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A good sun-protective hat&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Several bathing suits (remember a strapless bikini or suit if you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t want unruly tan lines)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A beach cover-up&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Planned outfits for special events like a welcome dinner, rehearsal dinner or farewell brunch&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A selection of mix and match day and nighttime outfits that make you look your best, yet are lightweight, comfortable and cool (skits, capris, shorts, tees, tank tops, etc.). Solid colors work well as do non-wrinkling fabrics&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A cardigan\/jacket for night time&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Exercise clothes and running shoes&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A purse\/evening bag&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A beach bag&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A daypack (for outings, trips)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A Spanish\/Creole phrasebook&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Good books and magazines for beach reading&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Toiletries and Cosmetics&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding make-up&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;High-SPF waterproof sunscreen&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;After-sun lotion or aloe vera gel&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Insect repellant&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Mini medical kit: pain killers, antacid tabs, anti-nausea pills, etc. It\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s best to be prepared for anything&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Ample toiletries (don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t count on the resort having what you want): toothpaste, toothbrush, deodorant (clear deodorant for the wedding day), cosmetics, makeup remover,&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;cotton swabs, Q-tips, shampoo &amp;amp; conditioner, moisturizer, mouthwash, comb &amp;amp; brush, nail&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;clippers, shaving cream, razors, hair dryer, tampons\/pads, etc.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Hair dryer\/straightener&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Curling iron\/curlers&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Wedding Things&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Any special personal touches you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122d like to add to the ceremony&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Gifts for wedding party\/family members&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A journal or diary (so you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t forget the experience)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Something old, something new, something borrowed, something blue&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;A good camera (to capture the moments) and film (if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re not digital)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Welcome bags &amp;amp; contents including weekend itineraries&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;CDs\/music&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Cake topper&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Printed materials: menus, programs, seating cards, signage&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Table decorations (disposable cameras, candles, etc.)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Guest book &amp;amp; pens&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Ceremony accessories (unity candle, Ketubah, ring-bearer pillow, etc.)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Thank-you notes\/gifts to vendors (including tip envelopes)&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Fix-it kit: Extras of all materials used to make favors, welcome bags, etc.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;li&gt; &lt;span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family: cambria,serif;\"&gt;Your wedding planning folder with all the details of your arrangements&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1754155,"PostDate":1367609862,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Totally normal Melissa14!! Try spreading out some of the items between your bridal party (isn't that what they are there for?!) to lower the number of additional bags you will have to bring. I'll share with you the packing list that we give to our clients as well so you can cross reference!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Happy Planning!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Carry-on items<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding dress. Don't trust your dress to checked luggage. Most airplanes have coat closets and will allow travelers to hang garment bags. Call ahead, let them know you will be bringing a dress and ask if the airline will let you hang your dress in the closet<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Groom\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s wedding outfit (tux, suit, shorts, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">All original and notarized documents--including air tickets, birth certificates, passports, hotel reservation confirmation, medical\/trip insurance, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Two sets of photocopies of all of the above documents<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your credit cards and ATM cards<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Phone numbers for your doctor, house\/pet sitter and credit card companies (in case your cards are lost or stolen)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Prescription medicine (in the original bottle)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding rings<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding vows<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your veil<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Bridal jewelry<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A change of clothes for the first day (just in case), including a bathing suit<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Copies of all contracts and vendor contact sheets<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Checked items<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Personal<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Special hosiery or undergarments<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding night sleepwear<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A variety of shoes (flip flops, heels, running shoes\/walking shoes, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Tiara or headpiece<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Garter<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Sunglasses<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A good sun-protective hat<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Several bathing suits (remember a strapless bikini or suit if you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t want unruly tan lines)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A beach cover-up<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Planned outfits for special events like a welcome dinner, rehearsal dinner or farewell brunch<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A selection of mix and match day and nighttime outfits that make you look your best, yet are lightweight, comfortable and cool (skits, capris, shorts, tees, tank tops, etc.). Solid colors work well as do non-wrinkling fabrics<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A cardigan\/jacket for night time<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Exercise clothes and running shoes<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A purse\/evening bag<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A beach bag<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A daypack (for outings, trips)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A Spanish\/Creole phrasebook<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Good books and magazines for beach reading<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Toiletries and Cosmetics<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding make-up<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">High-SPF waterproof sunscreen<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">After-sun lotion or aloe vera gel<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Insect repellant<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Mini medical kit: pain killers, antacid tabs, anti-nausea pills, etc. It\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s best to be prepared for anything<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Ample toiletries (don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t count on the resort having what you want): toothpaste, toothbrush, deodorant (clear deodorant for the wedding day), cosmetics, makeup remover,<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">cotton swabs, Q-tips, shampoo & conditioner, moisturizer, mouthwash, comb & brush, nail<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">clippers, shaving cream, razors, hair dryer, tampons\/pads, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Hair dryer\/straightener<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Curling iron\/curlers<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding Things<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Any special personal touches you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122d like to add to the ceremony<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Gifts for wedding party\/family members<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A journal or diary (so you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t forget the experience)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Something old, something new, something borrowed, something blue<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A good camera (to capture the moments) and film (if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re not digital)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Welcome bags & contents including weekend itineraries<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">CDs\/music<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Cake topper<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Printed materials: menus, programs, seating cards, signage<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Table decorations (disposable cameras, candles, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Guest book & pens<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Ceremony accessories (unity candle, Ketubah, ring-bearer pillow, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Thank-you notes\/gifts to vendors (including tip envelopes)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Fix-it kit: Extras of all materials used to make favors, welcome bags, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your wedding planning folder with all the details of your arrangements<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"laura@luxedestinationweddings.com ","IpAddress":"","GroupId":44,"GroupName":"Vendor","JoinDate":1304622690,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-239674.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":145,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Jessica4LUXE","Id":239674,"Name":"Jessica4LUXE","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cb4b395086409c1abc1455b725e1b2ff","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1754158,"PostDate":1367610440,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><em><span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span>Marrying My 5th Grade \"Boyfriend\"...Life has a funny way of working itself out <span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"trina2103@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"98.154.15.214","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1340652630,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257115.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Melissa14","Id":257115,"Name":"Melissa14","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0bc8fd4d74f4af106988350969c59636","RawContent":"[quote]<p>Originally Posted by [b]Jessica4LUXE[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Totally normal Melissa14!! Try spreading out some of the items between your bridal party (isn&#039;t that what they are there for?!) to lower the number of additional bags you will have to bring. I&#039;ll share with you the packing list that we give to our clients as well so you can cross reference! \n \n Happy Planning! \n \n [b][size=3][font=cambria]Carry-on items[\/font][\/size][\/b] [list]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding dress. Don&#039;t trust your dress to checked luggage. Most airplanes have coat closets and will allow travelers to hang garment bags. Call ahead, let them know you will be bringing a dress and ask if the airline will let you hang your dress in the closet[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Groom\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s wedding outfit (tux, suit, shorts, etc.)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]All original and notarized documents--including air tickets, birth certificates, passports, hotel reservation confirmation, medical\/trip insurance, etc.[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Two sets of photocopies of all of the above documents[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Your credit cards and ATM cards[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Phone numbers for your doctor, house\/pet sitter and credit card companies (in case your cards are lost or stolen)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Prescription medicine (in the original bottle)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding rings[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding vows[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Your veil[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Bridal jewelry[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A change of clothes for the first day (just in case), including a bathing suit[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Copies of all contracts and vendor contact sheets[\/font][\/size]\n[\/list] [b][size=3][font=cambria]Checked items[\/font][\/size][\/b] \n [b][size=3][font=cambria]Personal[\/font][\/size][\/b] [list]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Special hosiery or undergarments[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding night sleepwear[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A variety of shoes (flip flops, heels, running shoes\/walking shoes, etc.)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Tiara or headpiece[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Garter[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Sunglasses[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A good sun-protective hat[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Several bathing suits (remember a strapless bikini or suit if you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t want unruly tan lines)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A beach cover-up[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Planned outfits for special events like a welcome dinner, rehearsal dinner or farewell brunch[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A selection of mix and match day and nighttime outfits that make you look your best, yet are lightweight, comfortable and cool (skits, capris, shorts, tees, tank tops, etc.). Solid colors work well as do non-wrinkling fabrics[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A cardigan\/jacket for night time[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Exercise clothes and running shoes[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A purse\/evening bag[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A beach bag[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A daypack (for outings, trips)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A Spanish\/Creole phrasebook[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Good books and magazines for beach reading[\/font][\/size]\n[\/list] [b][size=3][font=cambria]Toiletries and Cosmetics[\/font][\/size][\/b] [list]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding make-up[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]High-SPF waterproof sunscreen[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]After-sun lotion or aloe vera gel[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Insect repellant[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Mini medical kit: pain killers, antacid tabs, anti-nausea pills, etc. It\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s best to be prepared for anything[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Ample toiletries (don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t count on the resort having what you want): toothpaste, toothbrush, deodorant (clear deodorant for the wedding day), cosmetics, makeup remover,[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]cotton swabs, Q-tips, shampoo &amp;amp; conditioner, moisturizer, mouthwash, comb &amp;amp; brush, nail[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]clippers, shaving cream, razors, hair dryer, tampons\/pads, etc.[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Hair dryer\/straightener[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Curling iron\/curlers[\/font][\/size]\n[\/list] [b][size=3][font=cambria]Wedding Things[\/font][\/size][\/b] [list]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Any special personal touches you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122d like to add to the ceremony[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Gifts for wedding party\/family members[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A journal or diary (so you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t forget the experience)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Something old, something new, something borrowed, something blue[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]A good camera (to capture the moments) and film (if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re not digital)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Welcome bags &amp;amp; contents including weekend itineraries[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]CDs\/music[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Cake topper[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Printed materials: menus, programs, seating cards, signage[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Table decorations (disposable cameras, candles, etc.)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Guest book &amp;amp; pens[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Ceremony accessories (unity candle, Ketubah, ring-bearer pillow, etc.)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Thank-you notes\/gifts to vendors (including tip envelopes)[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Fix-it kit: Extras of all materials used to make favors, welcome bags, etc.[\/font][\/size]\n[*][size=3][font=cambria]Your wedding planning folder with all the details of your arrangements[\/font][\/size]\n[\/list][\/quote] \n Great List. Thanks.","Attachments":[],"Id":1754186,"PostDate":1367614478,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Jessica4LUXE<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Totally normal Melissa14!! Try spreading out some of the items between your bridal party (isn't that what they are there for?!) to lower the number of additional bags you will have to bring. I'll share with you the packing list that we give to our clients as well so you can cross reference!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Happy Planning!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Carry-on items<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding dress. Don't trust your dress to checked luggage. Most airplanes have coat closets and will allow travelers to hang garment bags. Call ahead, let them know you will be bringing a dress and ask if the airline will let you hang your dress in the closet<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Groom\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s wedding outfit (tux, suit, shorts, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">All original and notarized documents--including air tickets, birth certificates, passports, hotel reservation confirmation, medical\/trip insurance, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Two sets of photocopies of all of the above documents<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your credit cards and ATM cards<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Phone numbers for your doctor, house\/pet sitter and credit card companies (in case your cards are lost or stolen)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Prescription medicine (in the original bottle)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding rings<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding vows<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your veil<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Bridal jewelry<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A change of clothes for the first day (just in case), including a bathing suit<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Copies of all contracts and vendor contact sheets<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Checked items<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Personal<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Special hosiery or undergarments<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding night sleepwear<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A variety of shoes (flip flops, heels, running shoes\/walking shoes, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Tiara or headpiece<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Garter<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Sunglasses<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A good sun-protective hat<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Several bathing suits (remember a strapless bikini or suit if you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t want unruly tan lines)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A beach cover-up<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Planned outfits for special events like a welcome dinner, rehearsal dinner or farewell brunch<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A selection of mix and match day and nighttime outfits that make you look your best, yet are lightweight, comfortable and cool (skits, capris, shorts, tees, tank tops, etc.). Solid colors work well as do non-wrinkling fabrics<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A cardigan\/jacket for night time<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Exercise clothes and running shoes<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A purse\/evening bag<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A beach bag<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A daypack (for outings, trips)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A Spanish\/Creole phrasebook<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Good books and magazines for beach reading<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Toiletries and Cosmetics<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding make-up<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">High-SPF waterproof sunscreen<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">After-sun lotion or aloe vera gel<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Insect repellant<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Mini medical kit: pain killers, antacid tabs, anti-nausea pills, etc. It\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s best to be prepared for anything<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Ample toiletries (don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t count on the resort having what you want): toothpaste, toothbrush, deodorant (clear deodorant for the wedding day), cosmetics, makeup remover,<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">cotton swabs, Q-tips, shampoo & conditioner, moisturizer, mouthwash, comb & brush, nail<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">clippers, shaving cream, razors, hair dryer, tampons\/pads, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Hair dryer\/straightener<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Curling iron\/curlers<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <strong><span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Wedding Things<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/p> <ul> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Any special personal touches you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122d like to add to the ceremony<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Gifts for wedding party\/family members<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A journal or diary (so you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t forget the experience)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Something old, something new, something borrowed, something blue<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">A good camera (to capture the moments) and film (if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re not digital)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Welcome bags & contents including weekend itineraries<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">CDs\/music<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Cake topper<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Printed materials: menus, programs, seating cards, signage<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Table decorations (disposable cameras, candles, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Guest book & pens<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Ceremony accessories (unity candle, Ketubah, ring-bearer pillow, etc.)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Thank-you notes\/gifts to vendors (including tip envelopes)<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Fix-it kit: Extras of all materials used to make favors, welcome bags, etc.<\/span><\/span><\/li> <li> <span  style=\"font-size: 12pt\"><span  style=\"font-family: cambria,serif\">Your wedding planning folder with all the details of your arrangements<\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <\/blockquote> <p> Great List. Thanks.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mbain86@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"99.240.164.37","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1339434769,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-256515.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"MelB2012","Id":256515,"Name":"MelB2012","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4c3ac913eb31b7a842623f15b6a95d32","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Great list Jessica!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1761455,"PostDate":1369602233,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Great list Jessica!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jandp.wedding@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1369302443,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-269886.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Miss J","Id":269886,"Name":"Miss J","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"091ecce52f06971639159bb716d608c8","RawContent":"Great list. Thank you!","Attachments":[],"Id":1761460,"PostDate":1369604573,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Great list. Thank you!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mcdonaldmom@sbcglobal.net","IpAddress":"70.247.50.216","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1368824444,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-269680.jpg?_r=1420816932","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"tmcdonald","Id":269680,"Name":"tmcdonald","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1e1929b512c208c41f9829102b395073","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; We just came back from our honeymoon a few days ago. Getting there and even back wasn&#039;t super easy but we certainly made it through. Here are my suggestions from learnings-&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The zipper on my David&#039;s Bridal dress bag broke after flight #1. This resulted in all kinds of trauma including my bonked head and a lost veil. I&#039;m not sure how often this happens, but maybe bring some bobby pins in your carry on to pin it back together if this happens, or maybe even a cheap backup dress bag. You don&#039;t want your dress dragging the floor, or items like your veil falling out of the bag, plus you don&#039;t want your groom to see the dress!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Sand will get you pulled over going through security. I tried to bring my sand ceremony back in my carry on. It was too precious to get broke. But when security ran the test on the substance to see what it was they messed up the look of the sand, it had a beautiful layering and now that is gone. I will have to buy more sand and re-pour it to get the colors to blend again like they should. I should have had them scoop it from the top, but mostly security doesn&#039;t care. I still wouldn&#039;t change putting it in my carry on. I can handle re-pouring sand I cant handle it breaking.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Bring bubble wrap for the return trip&amp;nbsp;and wrap anything that can break very well both there and back. They throw the bags around!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1761665,"PostDate":1369687131,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> We just came back from our honeymoon a few days ago. Getting there and even back wasn't super easy but we certainly made it through. Here are my suggestions from learnings-<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The zipper on my David's Bridal dress bag broke after flight #1. This resulted in all kinds of trauma including my bonked head and a lost veil. I'm not sure how often this happens, but maybe bring some bobby pins in your carry on to pin it back together if this happens, or maybe even a cheap backup dress bag. You don't want your dress dragging the floor, or items like your veil falling out of the bag, plus you don't want your groom to see the dress!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sand will get you pulled over going through security. I tried to bring my sand ceremony back in my carry on. It was too precious to get broke. But when security ran the test on the substance to see what it was they messed up the look of the sand, it had a beautiful layering and now that is gone. I will have to buy more sand and re-pour it to get the colors to blend again like they should. I should have had them scoop it from the top, but mostly security doesn't care. I still wouldn't change putting it in my carry on. I can handle re-pouring sand I cant handle it breaking.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Bring bubble wrap for the return trip\u00a0and wrap anything that can break very well both there and back. They throw the bags around!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jedoyle78@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"75.120.137.199","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1335539426,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-254605.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"MSPOKRAN","Id":254605,"Name":"MSPOKRAN","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"97de8f1c0644cbfab3b9e13df4de352c","RawContent":"That&#039;s one I had not thought of.....bubble wrap. Great idea. Writing it in my notebook.","Attachments":[],"Id":1761716,"PostDate":1369701392,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                That's one I had not thought of.....bubble wrap. Great idea. Writing it in my notebook.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mcdonaldmom@sbcglobal.net","IpAddress":"70.247.50.216","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1368824444,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-269680.jpg?_r=1420816932","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"tmcdonald","Id":269680,"Name":"tmcdonald","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"142b480793fc5c13eb1fe8168229c15f","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]MSPOKRAN[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n We just came back from our honeymoon a few days ago. Getting there and even back wasn&#039;t super easy but we certainly made it through. Here are my suggestions from learnings- \n \n The zipper on my David&#039;s Bridal dress bag broke after flight #1. This resulted in all kinds of trauma including my bonked head and a lost veil. I&#039;m not sure how often this happens, but maybe bring some bobby pins in your carry on to pin it back together if this happens, or maybe even a cheap backup dress bag. You don&#039;t want your dress dragging the floor, or items like your veil falling out of the bag, plus you don&#039;t want your groom to see the dress! \n \n Sand will get you pulled over going through security. I tried to bring my sand ceremony back in my carry on. It was too precious to get broke. But when security ran the test on the substance to see what it was they messed up the look of the sand, it had a beautiful layering and now that is gone. I will have to buy more sand and re-pour it to get the colors to blend again like they should. I should have had them scoop it from the top, but mostly security doesn&#039;t care. I still wouldn&#039;t change putting it in my carry on. I can handle re-pouring sand I cant handle it breaking. \n \n Bring bubble wrap for the return trip and wrap anything that can break very well both there and back. They throw the bags around![\/quote] \n \n OMG! I&#039;ve been so stressed about my stupid sand ceremony frame. I have this whole thing set up where everyone will pour the sand at the bottom of our frame and then we will pour a layer of two colors on top and I have no clue how I am going to get that back home without breaking it. Also, because I don&#039;t want to pay $50 for an ugly sand frame I am making my own from a simple shadow box frame and it isn&#039;t completely sealed all the way. Yikes!","Attachments":[],"Id":1762095,"PostDate":1369789063,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>MSPOKRAN<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> We just came back from our honeymoon a few days ago. Getting there and even back wasn't super easy but we certainly made it through. Here are my suggestions from learnings-<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The zipper on my David's Bridal dress bag broke after flight #1. This resulted in all kinds of trauma including my bonked head and a lost veil. I'm not sure how often this happens, but maybe bring some bobby pins in your carry on to pin it back together if this happens, or maybe even a cheap backup dress bag. You don't want your dress dragging the floor, or items like your veil falling out of the bag, plus you don't want your groom to see the dress!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Sand will get you pulled over going through security. I tried to bring my sand ceremony back in my carry on. It was too precious to get broke. But when security ran the test on the substance to see what it was they messed up the look of the sand, it had a beautiful layering and now that is gone. I will have to buy more sand and re-pour it to get the colors to blend again like they should. I should have had them scoop it from the top, but mostly security doesn't care. I still wouldn't change putting it in my carry on. I can handle re-pouring sand I cant handle it breaking.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Bring bubble wrap for the return trip\u00a0and wrap anything that can break very well both there and back. They throw the bags around!<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> OMG! I've been so stressed about my stupid sand ceremony frame. I have this whole thing set up where everyone will pour the sand at the bottom of our frame and then we will pour a layer of two colors on top and I have no clue how I am going to get that back home without breaking it. Also, because I don't want to pay $50 for an ugly sand frame I am making my own from a simple shadow box frame and it isn't completely sealed all the way. Yikes!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><em><span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span>Marrying My 5th Grade \"Boyfriend\"...Life has a funny way of working itself out <span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/em><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"trina2103@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"98.154.15.214","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1340652630,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257115.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Melissa14","Id":257115,"Name":"Melissa14","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":73813,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"152a62511214236613ff2225fa744832","RawContent":"Great packing list!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1762808,"PostDate":1369957909,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Great packing list!!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jenandcasey2014@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"71.47.3.153","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1359696677,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265472.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":160,"PhotoHeight":160,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ucfjennifer","Id":265472,"Name":"ucfjennifer","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"73813","Title":"Packing Anxiety","LastPostDate":1413048118},"Pages":{"TotalItems":24,"TotalPages":3,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":20},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
