Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"198.137.185.16","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1426169918,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f4d27fdd7c90516d87fe582556c0a563","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;For the welcome letter - I am putting a general Welcome to Mexico - and then listing the events like our welcome cocktail party - the basic timeline for the wedding day and the schedule for our group trip to Xcaret.&amp;nbsp; I am also including our request about social media and photo sharing.&amp;nbsp; I don&#039;t want to look at my guests and see a bunch of phones in front of faces, so I am asking that nobody have phones out during the ceremony.&amp;nbsp; During the reception they can snap away but I will ask that they not share those on social media till I have had a chance to share some.&amp;nbsp; I am thinking we might need a wedding hashtag so we can see everyone&#039;s after the fact.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For the program- I&#039;m doing fan programs, since it will be pretty warm.&amp;nbsp; Then I will list who is who in the wedding party - the timeline for the ceremony - cocktail hour etc. (since there now has to be a big break between ceremony and cocktail hour)&amp;nbsp; I want to note what time the photobooth will open and that sort of thing and I will list the menu there since I&#039;m not doing menu cards.&amp;nbsp; I&#039;m going to put a reminder on the program also that goes something like:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;\t\t The Bride &amp;amp; Groom would like you to be fully present during the ceremony, and have hired professional to capture this joyous day.&amp;nbsp; While we appreciate you wanting to help us document this special event, please keep your cameras and phones silent and put away until after the I do&#039;s unless you have been specifically asked by the Bride &amp;amp; Groom to do otherwise&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;My timeline looks like this right now - might have to move a couple little things still but:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;2:30 PM Photographer and Videographers begin &amp;nbsp; Photos of Guys getting ready&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;3:00 PM Detail Shots (Dress hanging, shoes, rings, etc.) &amp;nbsp; Photos of Girls getting ready - hair and makeup done by 3:45&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;3:45 PM Guests begin seating&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;3:50 AM Couple first look photos&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;4:00 PM Ceremony&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;4:35 PM Champagne toast&amp;nbsp; &amp;amp; Group Photo - Everyone Attending &amp;nbsp; Photos for wedding party and family&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;6:00 PM Cocktail Hour begins &amp;nbsp; DJ starts music&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;7:00 PM Reception Starts&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;7:10 PM Dinner Served&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;7:25 PM Speaches\/Toasts&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;7:50 PM Cut the cake&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;8:00 PM First Dance &amp;nbsp; Photo Booth Opens&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;8:10 PM Pictures with Sparklers on Beach&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;8:30 PM Photographer Finishes&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;9:30 PM Videotgrapher Finishes&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;10:00 PM DJ Finishes &amp;nbsp; PhotoBooth Closes &amp;nbsp; Reception Ends&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889077,"PostDate":1426169797,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>For the welcome letter - I am putting a general Welcome to Mexico - and then listing the events like our welcome cocktail party - the basic timeline for the wedding day and the schedule for our group trip to Xcaret.\u00a0 I am also including our request about social media and photo sharing.\u00a0 I don't want to look at my guests and see a bunch of phones in front of faces, so I am asking that nobody have phones out during the ceremony.\u00a0 During the reception they can snap away but I will ask that they not share those on social media till I have had a chance to share some.\u00a0 I am thinking we might need a wedding hashtag so we can see everyone's after the fact.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For the program- I'm doing fan programs, since it will be pretty warm.\u00a0 Then I will list who is who in the wedding party - the timeline for the ceremony - cocktail hour etc. (since there now has to be a big break between ceremony and cocktail hour)\u00a0 I want to note what time the photobooth will open and that sort of thing and I will list the menu there since I'm not doing menu cards.\u00a0 I'm going to put a reminder on the program also that goes something like:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Bride & Groom would like you to be fully present during the ceremony, and have hired professional to capture this joyous day.\u00a0 While we appreciate you wanting to help us document this special event, please keep your cameras and phones silent and put away until after the I do's unless you have been specifically asked by the Bride & Groom to do otherwise<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My timeline looks like this right now - might have to move a couple little things still but:<\/p>\n<p>2:30 PM Photographer and Videographers begin \u00a0 Photos of Guys getting ready<\/p>\n<p>3:00 PM Detail Shots (Dress hanging, shoes, rings, etc.) \u00a0 Photos of Girls getting ready - hair and makeup done by 3:45<\/p>\n<p>3:45 PM Guests begin seating<\/p>\n<p>3:50 AM Couple first look photos\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>4:00 PM Ceremony<\/p>\n<p>4:35 PM Champagne toast\u00a0 & Group Photo - Everyone Attending \u00a0 Photos for wedding party and family<\/p>\n<p>6:00 PM Cocktail Hour begins \u00a0 DJ starts music<\/p>\n<p>7:00 PM Reception Starts<\/p>\n<p>7:10 PM Dinner Served<\/p>\n<p>7:25 PM Speaches\/Toasts<\/p>\n<p>7:50 PM Cut the cake<\/p>\n<p>8:00 PM First Dance \u00a0 Photo Booth Opens<\/p>\n<p>8:10 PM Pictures with Sparklers on Beach<\/p>\n<p>8:30 PM Photographer Finishes<\/p>\n<p>9:30 PM Videotgrapher Finishes<\/p>\n<p>10:00 PM DJ Finishes \u00a0 PhotoBooth Closes \u00a0 Reception Ends<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"karinbean@pgatourhq.com","IpAddress":"67.190.225.116","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1363558492,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-267461.jpg?_r=1420723355","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JaxBchKay","Id":267461,"Name":"JaxBchKay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"167.206.146.147","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"febcbb22f34b9ad8e79c876dd58c76ec","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone. I haven&#039;t really looked too much throughout this thread but I have a question about this resort. I am getting married here August 15th. Is everyone getting 1-2 options for their entrees for the reception. We were told we can have one, but if we want two choices, we have to get everyones choice prior to the wedding. I am trying to figure out how to put this into my RSVPs and get peoples responses without being tacky. Also, lets say we choice beef and chicken, what if people have an allergy or do not eat seafood, I will need to have an option for them to write it somewhere and I just feel like it will look wierd. Will the resort prepare something for those people that cannot eat either of the choices I have? I Am stressing majorly about it but I don&#039;t want to anymore. I want to order my invites and either make and RSVP card that suits this purpose, or make a website where they can select from some sort of drop down menu. I don&#039;t know! Please give suggestions!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889839,"PostDate":1426695743,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi everyone. I haven't really looked too much throughout this thread but I have a question about this resort. I am getting married here August 15th. Is everyone getting 1-2 options for their entrees for the reception. We were told we can have one, but if we want two choices, we have to get everyones choice prior to the wedding. I am trying to figure out how to put this into my RSVPs and get peoples responses without being tacky. Also, lets say we choice beef and chicken, what if people have an allergy or do not eat seafood, I will need to have an option for them to write it somewhere and I just feel like it will look wierd. Will the resort prepare something for those people that cannot eat either of the choices I have? I Am stressing majorly about it but I don't want to anymore. I want to order my invites and either make and RSVP card that suits this purpose, or make a website where they can select from some sort of drop down menu. I don't know! Please give suggestions!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lornj29@aim.com","IpAddress":"68.192.37.147","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1410109020,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"lornj29","Id":279723,"Name":"lornj29","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"159.18.168.14","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e55be74042afc3819bae2af4e25aced2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"lornj29\"] We are booked at Now Sapphire for April 2016. We were told we would get 2 main course choices with either the Eternity or Divine packages. Not sure about other packages.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The WC told me that the best way to identify who gets what for food is to color-code the place cards - so red for chicken, green for beef and blue for other, or something like that. They should be able to accommodate special requests. I did ask about that, as I have some vegetarians &amp;amp; celiacs (gluten-free) among our guests. On the form we need submit about 1 month before the wedding, it does ask:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;10. Do you have allergic or vegetarian people in your group? How many? Please write their names.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;However, again, that seems to only apply to private dinners, so not sure if it applies to you. I haven&#039;t thought far enough ahead as to how I&#039;m going to get guests&#039; meal selections in advance. I am using a Google Form to capture RSVPs and have asked for dietary restrictions there, so at least I have that covered.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889871,"PostDate":1426707449,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"279723\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/279723-lornj29\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">lornj29<\/span><\/a> We are booked at Now Sapphire for April 2016. We were told we would get 2 main course choices with either the Eternity or Divine packages. Not sure about other packages.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The WC told me that the best way to identify who gets what for food is to color-code the place cards - so red for chicken, green for beef and blue for other, or something like that. They should be able to accommodate special requests. I did ask about that, as I have some vegetarians & celiacs (gluten-free) among our guests. On the form we need submit about 1 month before the wedding, it does ask:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>10. Do you have allergic or vegetarian people in your group? How many? Please write their names.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>However, again, that seems to only apply to private dinners, so not sure if it applies to you. I haven't thought far enough ahead as to how I'm going to get guests' meal selections in advance. I am using a Google Form to capture RSVPs and have asked for dietary restrictions there, so at least I have that covered.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ekjzwedding@gmail.com","IpAddress":"24.85.127.174","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1417449445,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281283.jpg?_r=1428779369","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"vancouverpetunia","Id":281283,"Name":"vancouverpetunia","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"67.71.84.110","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1426770187,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"49d9c6e6a20b038284d786a64d4153ba","RawContent":"[quote name=\"lornj29\" post=\"1889839\" timestamp=\"1426695743\"]\nHi everyone. I haven&#039;t really looked too much throughout this thread but I have a question about this resort. I am getting married here August 15th. Is everyone getting 1-2 options for their entrees for the reception. We were told we can have one, but if we want two choices, we have to get everyones choice prior to the wedding. I am trying to figure out how to put this into my RSVPs and get peoples responses without being tacky. Also, lets say we choice beef and chicken, what if people have an allergy or do not eat seafood, I will need to have an option for them to write it somewhere and I just feel like it will look wierd. Will the resort prepare something for those people that cannot eat either of the choices I have? I Am stressing majorly about it but I don&#039;t want to anymore. I want to order my invites and either make and RSVP card that suits this purpose, or make a website where they can select from some sort of drop down menu. I don&#039;t know! Please give suggestions![\/quote]We put the meal selection on our RSVPs.  RSVP was done on our website through theknot.com.  We had a small wedding - most people did not RSVP and I had to call them to find out their choice.  With a group of 20 this was not a big deal.\n\nA heads up: The beef was wonderful!  The chicken was salty.  Every chicken dish I had the entire week was very salty.\nThe surf and Turf:\n[sharedmedia=gallery:images:72599] \n\nPhotos of our wedding:\n[sharedmedia=gallery:albums:17479]\n\nAlso, because our party was so small, I had a seating chart with all of the meal choices written out.  At our pre-wedding meeting, I gave the seating chart to Ramon with our personalized favors.  He placed them all for us and all dishes were delivered correctly.  With a bigger party you might want to have different colored place cards for different meal choices.  Make sure you highlight which is which to the wedding coordinator.  Alternatively you could put a small picture of a cow or chicken (or fish) in the corner of each if you want to keep the cards the same color.","Attachments":[],"Id":1889964,"PostDate":1426769957,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>lornj29, on 18 March 2015 - 08:22 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hi everyone. I haven't really looked too much throughout this thread but I have a question about this resort. I am getting married here August 15th. Is everyone getting 1-2 options for their entrees for the reception. We were told we can have one, but if we want two choices, we have to get everyones choice prior to the wedding. I am trying to figure out how to put this into my RSVPs and get peoples responses without being tacky. Also, lets say we choice beef and chicken, what if people have an allergy or do not eat seafood, I will need to have an option for them to write it somewhere and I just feel like it will look wierd. Will the resort prepare something for those people that cannot eat either of the choices I have? I Am stressing majorly about it but I don't want to anymore. I want to order my invites and either make and RSVP card that suits this purpose, or make a website where they can select from some sort of drop down menu. I don't know! Please give suggestions!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>We put the meal selection on our RSVPs.\u00a0 RSVP was done on our website through theknot.com.\u00a0 We had a small wedding - most people did not RSVP and I had to call them to find out their choice.\u00a0 With a group of 20 this was not a big deal.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>A heads up: The beef was wonderful!\u00a0 The chicken was salty.\u00a0 Every chicken dish I had the entire week was very salty.<\/p>\n<p>The surf and Turf:<\/p>\n<p><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/72599-surf-and-turf\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17479\/sml_gallery_257303_17479_347721.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Surf and Turf'  width='200' height='151'  alt='Surf and Turf' id='sml_image_view_72599' \/><\/a>\n<br \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div>Photos of our wedding:<\/div>\n<div><div class='_sharedMediaBbcode'>\n\t<div class='bbcode_mediaWrap clearfix'>\n\t\t<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/album\/17479-wedding-at-now-sapphire\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17479\/tn_gallery_257303_17479_317668.jpg' class='sharedmedia_screenshot cover_img_75' title='02'  width='75' height='75'  alt='02' id='tn_image_view_72593_cover' \/><\/a>\n\t\t<div class='details'>\n\t\t\t<h5><a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/album\/17479-wedding-at-now-sapphire\/' class='bbc_url' title=''>Album: Wedding at Now Sapphire<\/a><\/h5>\n\t\t\t<div>30 images<\/div>\n\t\t\t<div>0 comments<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>Also, because our party was so small, I had a seating chart with all of the meal choices written out.\u00a0 At our pre-wedding meeting, I gave the seating chart to Ramon with our personalized favors.\u00a0 He placed them all for us and all dishes were delivered correctly.\u00a0 With a bigger party you might want to have different colored place cards for different meal choices.\u00a0 Make sure you highlight which is which to the wedding coordinator.\u00a0 Alternatively you could put a small picture of a cow or chicken (or fish) in the corner of each if you want to keep the cards the same color.<\/div>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dinaskates84@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"74.12.203.194","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1341078220,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-257303.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"DinaQtobe","Id":257303,"Name":"DinaQtobe","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.202.225.11","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62152,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7529066c605c91e4360530b6c4e8a9a1","RawContent":"&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;We have a great new promotion for BDW Brides! &amp;nbsp;Book your wedding with Wright Travel Agency and fly FREE! &amp;nbsp;See below for more information.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89);\"&gt;Book 15 rooms or more at selected properties and receive free round trip coach air tickets.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(199,135,115);\"&gt;Book 3\/16\/2015-5\/31\/2015 for travel through 12\/31\/2016&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;For more information:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&lt;a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"mailto:info@wrighttravelagency.com\" title=\"External link\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(98,158,152);\"&gt;info@wrighttravelagency.com&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(89,89,89);\"&gt;Or&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;fill out our contact form:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;color:rgb(40,40,40);text-align:center;\"&gt;&lt;a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"https:\/\/www.wrighttravelagen